      "writtenOn": "2020-04-04T02:54:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the sequence of data from USB host to UART FIFO: When USB data comes from Host, then uart_written() shall be called in a config-\u003edeferred_rx() in usb-stream.c. uart_written() calls uartn_tx_start() to set GC_UART_ICTRL_TX_MASK and to trigger UART EC TX interrupt. UART-EC TX interrupt handler calls get_data_from_usb() to move data from USB data queue to UART TX FIFO.\n\nSince cr50 can know the data won\u0027t be pushed into UART TX FIFO, I thought it would be better to ignore them when they arrive and to skip calling uartn_tx_start().",
